{"name":"Cheese Wiz","hex":"#dfad51","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cheese","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dairy product made from curdled or cultured milk.","Any particular variety of cheese."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To prepare curds for making cheese.","To make holes in a pattern of circuitry to decrease pattern density."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheese"},{"term":"wiz","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who is exceptionally clever, gifted or skilled in a particular area.","A wizard (an administrator of a multi-user dungeon)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be promoted to wizard (administrator) status in a multi-user dungeon, by completing the game quest."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wiz"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cheez Whiz","blocks":[{"text":"Cheez Whiz is a brand of processed cheese sauce and spread produced by Kraft Foods. It was developed by a team led by food scientist Edwin Traisman (1915–2007). It was first sold in 1952, and, with some changes in formulation, continues to be in production today."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Cheezwhiz_kraft_logo.png/330px-Cheezwhiz_kraft_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheez_Whiz"},{"title":"Cheese","blocks":[{"text":"Cheese is a type of dairy product produced in a range of flavors, textures, and forms by curdling of milk, usually from cows, goats or sheep, and sometimes of water buffalo. During production, milk is usually acidified and either the enzymes of rennet or bacterial enzymes with similar activity are added to cause the protein casein to coagulate. The solid curds, consisting of proteins and milkfat, are then separated from the liquid whey and pressed into finished cheese. Some cheeses have aromatic molds on the outer layer or rind, while others have them throughout."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Cheese_platter.jpg/330px-Cheese_platter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheese"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Whiz_wit%27_Pat.gif/500px-Whiz_wit%27_Pat.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Whiz_wit%27_Pat.gif/500px-Whiz_wit%27_Pat.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWhiz_wit'_Pat.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Clara_Peeters_-_Still_Life_with_Cheeses%2C_Almonds_and_Pretzels.jpg/500px-Clara_Peeters_-_Still_Life_with_Cheeses%2C_Almonds_and_Pretzels.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Clara_Peeters_-_Still_Life_with_Cheeses%2C_Almonds_and_Pretzels.jpg/1280px-Clara_Peeters_-_Still_Life_with_Cheeses%2C_Almonds_and_Pretzels.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Clara_Peeters_-_Still_Life_with_Cheeses%2C_Almonds_and_Pretzels.jpg/500px-Clara_Peeters_-_Still_Life_with_Cheeses%2C_Almonds_and_Pretzels.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cheeses in art: Still Life with Cheeses, Almonds and Pretzels, Clara Peeters, c. 1615","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClara_Peeters_-_Still_Life_with_Cheeses%2C_Almonds_and_Pretzels.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/9-alimenti%2C_formaggi%2CTaccuino_Sanitatis%2C_Casanatense_4182..jpg/500px-9-alimenti%2C_formaggi%2CTaccuino_Sanitatis%2C_Casanatense_4182..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 